        <section id="ineffective-working-relationships-with-other-teams-and-departments"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>Ineffective working relationships with other teams and departments</h2>
              <p>What we tend to notice when working relationships with other departments and teams fail is the negative, adversarial and uncomfortable atmosphere. This negative work interaction also has a significant impact on innovation, which can cause severe damage to an organisation's productivity, efficiency, reputation and even survival. To truly understand the value of team and department collaboration let’s take a look at some of the potential consequences when this collaboration fails.</p>

              
              
<div class="gallery-container">
  <div role="group" class="gallery no-js">
    <ul>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Productivity and efficiency
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Failure to communicate and work together with other teams and departments has a huge impact on productivity and efficiency, which in turn directly affects the progress of a project. It’s hard to imagine a team that isn’t communicating, has no shared vision or sense of shared responsibility, working efficiently together to meet deadlines.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p2_slide1.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Talent retention
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>There is a huge demand for high quality developers and talent retention is key to a business’s success. If developers find that there is a lack of co-operation and communication, they will quickly move on to another company. The atmosphere created by a lack of communication and collaboration will only drive talent away. The resulting staff turnover can have a serious impact on project timelines and costs.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p2_slide2.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Innovation
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>For a company to stay relevant and on the cutting edge in any market, the employees must remain innovative. Failure to work effectively with other teams and departments significantly inhibits innovation. When a company falls behind in innovation it gets harder and harder to catch up, possibly even leading to the failure of the company.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p2_slide3.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Reduced collaboration
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Collaboration could become impossible if there is a lack of communication and effective working relationships. This in turn will prevent any kind of synergistic interaction between teams and departments.  It will also have a further impact on productivity and efficiency.</p>
<p>Without collaboration, innovation and creativity will become incredibly difficult, and its implementation will become unfeasible.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s4_p2_slide4.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
